page("texas-football-tailgate-grilling","Texas Football Tailgate Grilling With a Flat Pack Grill","Setting up a flat pack charcoal grill at a Texas football tailgate: lot rules, menu, timing, and safe ash handling.","full13",f"""
<p>Friday night lights, Saturday college games, Sunday pros: in Texas, the parking lot cook is part of the game. A flat pack grill that packs flat behind the seat is made for it.</p>
<h2>Before you go</h2>{ul(["Check the venue's tailgating rules. Many lots allow charcoal with conditions (ash containers, distance from vehicles); some don't allow open flames at all.","Prep at home: slice fajita meat, skewer, season, make sides.","Pack a lidded metal ash can, water, gloves, tongs and a thermometer."])}
<h2>Set up</h2>{ul(["On the pavement, away from the vehicle, fuel areas and foot traffic.","Never on a tailgate, plastic table or truck bed.","The Slot Grill's air gap (2⅞&quot; on the Compact, 3⅝&quot; on the Full Size) helps minimize radiant heat to the surface below, but it stays on non-combustible ground."])}
<h2>A tailgate menu that works</h2>{table(["Time to kickoff","Cook"],[["3 hours","Light coals; jalapeño poppers on the cool side"],["2 hours","Sausage links and fajitas"],["1 hour","Burgers or smash burgers on the griddle"],["Before you walk in","Let the fire burn down; ash into the metal can"]])}
<p>Recipes: {L("beef-fajitas-skirt-steak","fajitas")}, {L("texas-hot-links-and-smoked-sausage","links")}, {L("bacon-wrapped-jalapeno-poppers","poppers")}.</p>
""","trips",[("Can I leave a charcoal grill burning while I'm in the game?","No. Never leave a fire unattended. Let it burn out and handle ash per venue rules.")])

page("deer-camp-cooking-with-a-flat-pack-grill","Deer Camp Cooking With a Flat Pack Grill","Feeding a Texas deer lease on a flat pack charcoal grill: breakfast, venison, cast iron chili, and setting up camp safely.","full08",f"""
<p>Deer camp cooking is early breakfasts, late suppers, cold mornings and whatever you shot. A heavy steel grill that stays set up all weekend and packs flat on Sunday is right at home. Slot Grill's FAQ says either model can be left set up at camp with basic care, and that the Full Size handles appropriately sized cast iron.</p>
<h2>Camp menu</h2>{table(["Meal","On the grill"],[["Pre-dawn","{0}".format(L("breakfast-tacos-on-the-griddle","Breakfast tacos")),],["Lunch","Sausage on white bread"],["Supper","{0}, or chili in a Dutch oven".format(L("venison-backstrap-on-a-flat-pack-grill","Backstrap"))],["After dark","Keep a small fire going as a fire pit, where allowed"]])}
<h2>Camp setup</h2>{ul(["Bare ground or gravel, clear of the blind, tents, vehicles and dry grass.","Cover the grill or bring the grates in if rain's coming; oil the cooking surfaces.","Keep game cold; separate raw meat from ready-to-eat food."])}
<h2>Which grill</h2><p>The <a href="{FULL}">Full Size</a> (20.5&quot; × 11.25&quot; cooking area) feeds a camp; the <a href="{COMPACT}">Compact</a> suits one to three hunters or tight ATV space.</p>
""","trips",[])

page("lake-weekend-grilling-texas","Lake Weekend Grilling in Texas","Using a flat pack charcoal grill at Texas lakes: where to set up, boat safety, food for a lake day, and cleanup.","c07",f"""
<p>From the Highland Lakes to the East Texas reservoirs, a lake weekend means cooking on shore. A flat pack grill rides in the boat as cargo and comes out on the bank.</p>
<h2>Rules that matter</h2>{ul(["Never light a charcoal grill on a boat deck or near the boat. Slot Grill's FAQ says the same: carry it as cargo and cook on shore.","Check park and lake authority rules for fires and grills.","Cook on sand, gravel or bare dirt, away from dry vegetation."])}
<h2>Lake-day menu</h2>{ul(["{0}".format(L("redfish-on-the-half-shell","Fish on the half shell")) + " (works for many lake fish too)","Fajitas on the griddle","Grilled corn"])}
<h2>Cleanup</h2><p>Let ash cool, drown it if allowed, pack it out in a metal can. Wipe and oil the grill once home; lake humidity is hard on bare carbon steel.</p>
""","trips",[])

page("river-gravel-bar-cooking","River Trip and Gravel Bar Cooking","Cooking on a Texas river trip with a flat pack grill: gravel bar rules, packing it in a canoe or kayak, and leaving no trace.","c13",f"""
<p>Texas rivers like the Guadalupe, Frio, Brazos and Devils have a long tradition of gravel-bar camping, but rules vary by river, outfitter and landowner. Check before you go.</p>
<h2>Packing</h2>{ul(["The <a href='"+COMPACT+"'>Compact</a> packs about 1&quot; thick and weighs about 14 lb, so it slides into a canoe or kayak hatch.","Pack charcoal in a waterproof bag.","Bring a lidded metal can for ash; pack everything out."])}
<h2>On the bar</h2>{ul(["Set up on gravel or sand above the waterline, away from brush.","Keep it small. Don't build fire rings.","Drown ash and stir until cold; pack it out where required."])}
<p>Food that travels: precooked sausage, foil-packet vegetables, fish you catch (follow regulations).</p>
""","trips",[])

page("hill-country-camping-grill","Hill Country Camping With a Flat Pack Grill","Camping in the Texas Hill Country with a flat pack charcoal grill: park fire rules, wind, and a simple camp menu.","c28",f"""
<p>Hill Country camping brings limestone, cedar, dry summers and sudden wind. A flat pack grill is a tidy way to cook without a big campfire.</p>
<h2>Before you light</h2>{ul(["State parks and private campgrounds set fire rules; burn bans can restrict them. Check at check-in.","Use the site's grill area or bare ground; cedar and dry grass catch easily.","Wind picks up in the afternoon; cook early or late."])}
<h2>Camp menu</h2>{ul(["Night one: {0}".format(L("texas-ribeye-over-mesquite","ribeye over mesquite")),"Morning: {0}".format(L("breakfast-tacos-on-the-griddle","breakfast tacos")),"Night two: {0}".format(L("chicken-fajitas-on-a-griddle-plate","chicken fajitas"))])}
""","trips",[])

page("gulf-coast-beach-grilling","Gulf Coast Beach Grilling","Grilling on Texas Gulf Coast beaches with a flat pack charcoal grill: local rules, wind, sand and safe ash disposal.","c07",f"""
<p>Beach rules on the Texas coast vary by city, county and park, and some beaches restrict fires. Check the local beach rules before you pack charcoal.</p>
<h2>On the sand</h2>{ul(["Sand is non-combustible, but buried coals stay hot and burn bare feet. Never bury coals.","The Gulf breeze is constant: coal end into the wind, more fuel.","Keep the grill well back from dunes and vegetation."])}
<h2>Ash</h2><p>Drown, stir, and pack ash out in a metal can or use designated bins.</p>
<h2>After</h2><p>Salt air speeds rust on carbon steel. Rinse off salt spray with fresh water, dry over a few coals, then oil. See {L("carbon-steel-care-in-texas-humidity","care in Texas humidity")}.</p>
""","trips",[])
